<mujoco>

    <option gravity="0 0 -10" />

    <worldbody>

        <geom
            type="plane"
            size="5 5 0.1"
            rgba="247 247 229 1"
        />

        <body
            name="arm"
            pos="0 0 1">

            <joint
                name="hinge"
                type="hinge"
                axis="1 0 0"
            />

            <geom
                type="capsule"
                fromto="0 0 0 0 0 -0.5"
                size="0.03"
                rgba="1 0 0 1"
            />

        </body>

    </worldbody>


    <actuator>

        <motor
            joint="hinge"
            gear="10"
        />

    </actuator>


</mujoco>

<!-- 
actuator/motor: defines how control signals are translated into generalized forces (torques) applied to joints or tendons
F = gear * u, where F is final force or torque, gear is the gear ratio/scaling factor specified in XML, and u is the scalar control signal sent to the actuator (-1 <= u <= 1)

More on gear:
1-Dimensional: If a joint has a single degree of freedom, gear="N" multiplies the applied motor force by N, simulating a gearbox with a gear ratio of N
6-Dimensional: When actuating a complex body or freejoint, you can specify 6 numbers to assign independent force and torque multipliers for \([F_x, F_y, F_z, T_x, T_y, T_z]\)

body/joint/hinge: provides a single rotational degree of freedom (DoF) btween a body and its parent, typically functioning as a pivot or pin
-->